0|0@australia^1440241457#cubox8e:N3bu89$:Why replace them now at all? The F15 is only just starting to barely be replaced after being in service since the 70s, same with the F16. The FA-18 is still a functional multi-role fighter plane, along with the super hornet and we are not in great demand for a cutting edge plane to square off against the likes of Chinese 5th generation fighters which are still at least 10 years out from considering production. The F35 suffers significantly from an overburden of roles. They've tried to make a stealth plane, an air superiority fighter, a multi-role bomber and a SVTOL. It's run up cost, forced unwanted engineering compromises and prevented it from excelling in any of the roles it's been picked for, especially because of the VTOL compromises. In fact in this sense is suffer from much the same problem as the FA18, which as a multi-role bomber had to sacrifice metrics in speed, turning, climbing and operational range for the ability to carry heavier loads over shorter distances than the F15. The Pentagon should never had tried to replace 3 different aircraft roles with one design.
